# Zeff bug report: an error, Z0101

This file was written by `zeff report-bug` on your computer. Nothing has been sent
anywhere. Read it before you attach it to an issue: it holds statements of your script,
the names and types of your variables and the names of the files they were read from.
It holds no rows of your data.
A message is quoted as it was printed, and a message may name a value where it must (a
text that could not be converted, the levels of a group): read those lines too.

## What went wrong

The script stopped with an error:

    error[Z0101]: no variable `year` in `the frame`
     --> scripts/main.zeff:28:12
       |
    28 |     .where(year >= 2010 && age >= 18)
       |            ^^^^ not a variable of the frame
       |
       = help: the variables of `the frame` are: id, wage, hours, female, region, educ

## Zeff

- version: 0.8.0
- edition: preview
- platform: the test's machine

## The statements

The failing statement and the statements it depends on: 2 of the 74 statements of
`scripts/main.zeff` (lines 19 and 24). Run alone, they fail in the same way.

    use functions::robustness                             // functions/robustness.zeff, shown in section 6; use comes first
    seed(20261015)
    let wages = import("data/wages.csv",
                       na_values: [-99, -98],
                       types: {hours: Str},
                       names: snake)                      // "Gross Wage" becomes gross_wage
        .where(year >= 2010 && age >= 18)
        .add(lwage = log(gross_wage),
             exper2 = exper^2,
             hours = to(hours, Float),                    // "varies" becomes NA, with a warning
             industry = category(industry),
             edu = category(edu, levels: ["school", "college", "postgrad"], ordered: true),
             age_group = case {
                 age < 25 => "young",
                 age < 55 => "prime",
                 _        => "older",
             })
        .label(female, [0 => "male", 1 => "female"])
        .recode(industry, ["Mining" => "Other", "Utilities" => "Other"])
        .panel(unit: worker, time: year)

## The run

- seed: set at line 19, `seed(20261015)`
- warnings and notes before the failure: none

